-- FH MCP Bridge
--
-- Entry-file stub (issue #75, docs/adr/0018): everything but the two FH-mandated setup
-- calls below lives in bridgeSession.lua (the dialog UI, TCP listener, and Session
-- lifecycle — see that file's own header comment and CONTEXT.md's "Session"/"Bridge
-- plugin" entries) so Serena's symbol tools can cover it — `.fh_lua` files can't be
-- recognized by Serena's installed Lua language server integration, `.lua` files can.
-- This file can't shrink further than the two calls below plus one require(): FH's own
-- docs say fhSetStringEncoding "should never be used by modules", so it must stay a
-- direct call here, before any require().
--
-- Install: this source form is split into sibling modules (require()'d below, including
-- bridgeSession.lua) purely so each one can be unit-tested standalone outside FH where
-- possible (see bridge/README.md) and, for bridgeSession.lua, so Serena can navigate it.
-- It is not itself the installable artifact — FH's own plugin convention expects one
-- file, and install_fh_plugin can only write one file per call (see docs/adr/0009). Build
-- the single-file artifact with:
--   lua bridge/scripts/build.lua
-- then copy just bridge/dist/Claude MCP Bridge.fh_lua into FH's Plugins folder and load
-- it via Tools -> Plugins, same as any other plugin.

-- fhInitialise must be the first function this plugin calls, before even require()
-- (per FH's own docs) — "save_required" pops FH's own save-changes dialog (OK/Cancel)
-- the moment the plugin loads, ensuring the project is saved before any work happens
-- through it (issue #33). Cancel there ends the plugin immediately, before the dialog
-- below is ever built. Declares a minimum FH version of 7.0.0, matching the earliest
-- version this project already supports side-by-side (see README.md) — not a new
-- restriction, just what fhInitialise itself requires as its other two arguments.
fhInitialise(7, 0, 0, "save_required")

-- Force UTF-8 regardless of this file's own saved file encoding (confirmed live via
-- describe_project's contextInfo: CI_STRING_ENCODING reported "ANSI" on an unmodified
-- install). Without this, accented/non-ASCII names, places, etc. round-trip through the
-- FH API as ANSI and silently lose or mangle characters ANSI can't represent (FH help:
-- "String Encoding and Unicode") — a real risk for a genealogy tool. Must be called here,
-- in the main plugin script, before any require() below: FH's docs say
-- fhSetStringEncoding "should never be used by modules" (scripts loaded via require()),
-- and the current string encoding it sets is what every required module inherits for the
-- rest of the Session, per FH's "Special Handling for Modules" — module require() order
-- below doesn't matter as long as this precedes all of them, which it does.
fhSetStringEncoding("UTF-8")

-- Everything else — the dialog UI, TCP listener, and Session lifecycle — lives in
-- bridgeSession.lua (issue #75, docs/adr/0018). See that file's own header comment.
require("bridgeSession")
